# The Cloud Revolution (2006-2013)

## AWS launches EC2 (2006)

**Before:** "I need a server" -> 3 months, $50k

**After:** "I need a server" -> 5 minutes, $0.10/hour

```mermaid +render
flowchart LR
    subgraph Before["Before Cloud"]
        REQ["Request"] --> APPROVE["CFO Approval<br/>(2 weeks)"]
        APPROVE --> PROCURE["Procurement<br/>(4 weeks)"]
        PROCURE --> SHIP["Shipping<br/>(2 weeks)"]
        SHIP --> RACK["Racking<br/>(1 week)"]
        RACK --> CONFIG["Configuration<br/>(1 week)"]
    end

    subgraph After["After Cloud"]
        API["API Call"] --> RUNNING["Server Running<br/>(5 minutes)"]
    end
```

---

# Why Cloud Won

## The economic shift

<!-- column_layout: [1, 1] -->

<!-- column: 0 -->

**Own Hardware (Old Way)**

**Upfront cost:** $50k-500k

**Cost model:** CapEx
- Buy assets upfront
- Depreciation over time
- Sunk cost

**Time to deploy:** Weeks/months
- Budget approval
- Procurement
- Shipping
- Racking & cabling
- Configuration

**Scale up:** Buy more hardware
- 3-month lead time
- Guess capacity needs

**Scale down:** Sell hardware?
- Good luck!
- Stuck with it

**Maintenance:** Your problem
- 24/7 staff
- Hardware failures
- Upgrades

<!-- column: 1 -->

**Cloud (New Way)**

**Upfront cost:** $0

**Cost model:** OpEx
- Pay as you go
- $0.10/hour
- Stop paying when not using

**Time to deploy:** Minutes
- API call
- Server running
- That's it

**Scale up:** Click a button
- Instant
- No planning needed

**Scale down:** Stop paying
- Delete resources
- Immediate cost savings

**Maintenance:** Their problem
- Cloud provider handles
- SLA guarantees
- Automatic updates

**The killer feature:** Pay only for what you use

> "We used to buy hardware for peak load.
> Now we rent it for 2 hours on Black Friday."

<!-- reset_layout -->

---

# The Container Era (2013-Present)

## Docker changes everything

**The problem Docker solved:**

```
Developer: "It works on my machine!"
Operations: "Well, your machine isn't production."
Developer: "..."
Operations: "..."
Both: *angry silence*
```

**Docker's answer:** Ship your machine

```bash
# Before: Here's my code, good luck
scp app.py server:/app/

# After: Here's my entire environment
docker push myapp:v1
```

---

# The Three Eras Summarized

## The evolution of deployment

<!-- column_layout: [1, 1] -->

<!-- column: 0 -->

**1. Server Room Era (1990s-2000s)**

- Own hardware
- Manual deploys
- Months to scale

**2. Cloud Era (2006-2013)**

- Rent hardware
- Scripted deploys
- Minutes to scale

**3. Container Era (2013-present)**

- Abstract hardware
- Automated deploys
- Seconds to scale

<!-- column: 1 -->

| Era | Deploy Time | Scale Time | "Works on my machine" |
|-----|-------------|------------|----------------------|
| **Server Room** | Days/weeks | Months | "Figure it out" |
| **Cloud** | Hours | Minutes | "Check the config" |
| **Container** | Seconds | Seconds | Solved! |

