# Deployment Strategies

## How to update production safely

<!-- column_layout: [1, 1] -->

<!-- column: 0 -->

**1. Rolling Update**

- Replace instances one at a time
- v1 → v2 → v2 → v2
- Always some instances running

**How it works:**
1. Deploy v2 to one instance
2. Health check passes
3. Move to next instance
4. Repeat until all updated

**Pros:**
- ✓ No downtime
- ✓ Simple to implement

**Cons:**
- ✗ Slow rollback (undo each)
- ✗ Both versions running simultaneously

**Use case:** Standard deployments

<!-- column: 1 -->

**2. Blue-Green Deployment**

- Blue (v1): Currently live
- Green (v2): New version ready
- Flip switch → all traffic to Green

**How it works:**
1. Deploy v2 to Green (inactive)
2. Test Green thoroughly
3. Switch traffic: Blue → Green
4. Keep Blue as backup

**Pros:**
- ✓ Instant rollback (flip back)
- ✓ No mixed versions
- ✓ Easy to test

**Cons:**
- ✗ Double resources needed

**Use case:** Critical apps, instant rollback needed

<!-- reset_layout -->

**3. Canary Deployment:** v2 gets 10% traffic → Watch metrics → Gradually increase → 100%
- **Risk:** Lowest (catches issues early with small user %)
- **Use case:** Risk-averse, large user bases

